   "delta": ": '1y',\n}));\n\napp.get('/api/products', (req, res) => {\n  res.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=300');\n  res.json(products);\n});\n\n// SPA fallback: always revalidate the HTML shell\napp.use((req, res) => {\n  res.set('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');\n  res.sendFile('index.html', { root: 'dist' });\n});\n```\n\nCommon traps:\n\n- **Long-cached HTML.** Never give HTML a long `max-age`. Users get stuck on an old page that references asset hashes you've already deleted.\n- **Confusing `no-cache` and `no-store`.** `no-cache` doesn't mean \"don't cache.\" `no-store` does.\n- **Missing `Vary`.** If a response depends on a request header like `Accept-Language`, send a matching `Vary`. Otherwise a cache can serve one user's variant to another.\n- **Unverified headers.** Frameworks and CDNs often override what you set, so check the actual headers with `curl -I` or the DevTools Network panel.\n\nFor the full list of directives, see [MDN's Cache-Control reference](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cache-Control)."
